# Python Virtual Environment Rule

Never run Python tools (pip, python, tox, pytest, etc.) outside of a virtual environment. The only exception is creating the venv itself.

## Default venv location

Use `.venv` in the project root.

## Creating a venv (if `.venv` doesn't exist)

```bash
python -m venv .venv
```

## Activating before any Python command

On Windows (PowerShell):
```powershell
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

On Unix/macOS:
```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

## Workflow

1. Check if `.venv` exists; if not, create it.
2. Activate the venv.
3. Then run any Python tooling (pip install, python, tox, pytest, etc.).
